note %global `--agent` wraps the response in {ok,data,meta,summary,breadcrumbs}; `--json` stays the RAW API body and never changes
note %global `--dump-surface` prints this table one fact per line — it is the build gate's hook, not a user feature
note %global `--json` and `--agent` are alternatives — passing both is a usage error
note %global `--no-hints` drops the breadcrumb footer (so do `--quiet` and `--json`)
note %global `uku <command> --help --agent` emits this table as JSON, including these notes
note %global these are parsed ANYWHERE on the line, before the command
note account `--account <name>` is a GLOBAL flag, NOT a subcommand here: `uku --account main tasks list`
note account `add` is sugar for `uku auth login --account <name>`
note account run `uku account current` before any write — a sandbox and the real firm look identical in the output
note api METHOD and PATH are POSITIONAL, not flags: `uku api GET /api/v3/tasks`
note api `uku api --describe [resource]` prints the resource map — the fastest way for an agent to orient
note api this reaches every v3 endpoint, so prefer it over dropping to curl
note auth `--base` on `auth login` beats UKU_BASE_URL and the key is validated against THAT base before anything is stored
note auth `--shell` is shorthand for `--format shell`
note auth `print-header` prints a LIVE credential on stdout — never echo it back, never commit it; prefer `uku api`
note batch `uku batch` is not how you run a batch — that is `uku <res> create --batch @f.jsonl`
note batch reads the LOCAL ledger under $UKU_CONFIG_HOME/batches and sends no request
note clients --batch belongs to `create`; `uku clients list --batch` is a usage error, not a bulk read
note clients a write needs --yes when stdout is not a TTY (exit 4 otherwise)
note completions eval "$(uku completions zsh)" in your rc
note contracts read-only in the CLI; contract rows are ETag-guarded — see `uku help api` and the 428 rules
note doctor `--json` (the global flag) gives the whole report as JSON
note doctor exits 1 only when a REQUIRED check fails, never for a warning
note help `uku <command> --help` prints the same card
note help a topic with no card is a usage error, not an empty page
note invoices money needs an All-scope key — a `403 … scope` is the system working as designed, do not retry around it
note invoices there is no `uku invoices patch`; use `uku api PATCH /api/v3/invoices/<id>`
note me prints exactly what `uku auth status` prints — the identity behind the active key
note members read-only in the CLI — member writes go through `uku api`
note products read-only in the CLI; the API does accept `POST /api/v3/products` (needs `name`) — reach it with `uku api`
note projects read-only in the CLI; the API does accept `POST /api/v3/projects` (needs `name`) — reach it with `uku api`
note setup UKU_SETUP_AGENT=claude|cursor|codex|all|none picks the target; the default `auto` detects what is installed
note tasks `create` needs `title`; status/date/client_id are optional
note tasks a 428 on `POST /api/v3/tasks` is NOT healed — it is a collection POST with no id to read an ETag from
note time `create` needs task_id, person_id and start
note time `start` with no `end` is a RUNNING TIMER, not logged work — the CLI refuses duration-without-end before sending
note time there is NO `uku time patch` — use `uku api PATCH /api/v3/time-entries/<id>`
note update re-runs the installer for the newest RELEASE tag, checksum-verified; UKU_CHANNEL=main opts into the unverified rolling edge
note version identical to `uku --version`
